      "qa_note": "Re-audit 2026-08-15: Cross-checked all three wrecks against the WA Museum Maritime Archaeology Database. Fin: iron whaler, built 1881, 93 tons, driven ashore at anchor (museum record) vs. earlier sources describing an 1923 cyclone wreck — sources also disagree on whether the vessel was the Fin or a sister ship Fynd (per Stanbury 1984 research cited by the museum record). Zvir: steel screw steamer built 1900 (Priestman & Co, Sunderland), 100.2m, 3,353 gross tons, ran aground 27 Nov 1902 carrying sugar from Java to Port Adelaide — confirmed by 2 independent sources. SS Perth: iron passenger/cargo steamer built 1863 (Glasgow), 58.5m, ~499 tons, struck the reef 17 Sept 1887 en route Fremantle-Wyndham with 63 passengers — confirmed by 2 independent sources.",
